WEBVTT

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:01.994
- Previously on The O. C:
- She came back...

00:00:02.203 --> 00:00:03.496
...so I guess you're going home.

00:00:03.705 --> 00:00:05.998
- You're his mother.
- I'm a mess, not a mother.

00:00:06.207 --> 00:00:09.877
- You can't walk away.
- This way he ends up with a real mom.

00:00:10.962 --> 00:00:12.964
It's sweet that
you're concerned about this boy...

00:00:13.131 --> 00:00:15.508
...but you need to focus on the future,
which means Luke.

00:00:15.758 --> 00:00:17.385
She chose you.
You're the one she wants.

00:00:17.635 --> 00:00:19.595
- I wanna sail to Tahiti.
- You're taking this to Tahiti?

00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:21.347
- How much do you need?
- It's $100,000.

00:00:21.514 --> 00:00:24.517
The check that you guys gave Jimmy.
We needed that 100 grand.

00:00:24.726 --> 00:00:26.728
- Ryan's gonna stay with us now.
- Awesome.

00:00:26.894 --> 00:00:29.272
We just got in way over our heads.

00:00:34.527 --> 00:00:37.280
- Oh, really? You think so?
- I do.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.115
We'll see about that, monkey pox.

00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:44.162
So the pupil has become the teacher.

00:00:44.412 --> 00:00:47.498
- Hey, guys.
- Hey.

00:00:47.915 --> 00:00:49.042
Who died?

00:00:49.292 --> 00:00:51.669
Seth, we need to talk to Ryan.

00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:53.921
Okay.

00:00:54.047 --> 00:00:58.176
If this has to do with the rug, I want to
say that Ryan had nothing to do with it.

00:00:58.426 --> 00:00:59.886
What about the rug?

00:01:00.303 --> 00:01:01.888
I'm gonna go now.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.561
So...

00:01:10.063 --> 00:01:12.565
Kirsten and I went
to Child Services this morning...

00:01:12.815 --> 00:01:16.569
...and we told them
that we want you to stay with us.

00:01:18.071 --> 00:01:20.782
But there's a catch.
Because you're a minor...

00:01:20.948 --> 00:01:23.409
...the only way they're gonna
allow that to happen...

00:01:23.576 --> 00:01:26.829
...is if we assume
all legal responsibility for you.

00:01:28.456 --> 00:01:32.960
- I can't ask you guys to do that.
- You don't have to. We're asking you.

00:01:33.211 --> 00:01:36.923
We've all talked about it,
and we want to be your legal guardians.

00:01:37.715 --> 00:01:39.717
We want you to be part of the family.

00:01:40.343 --> 00:01:41.427
If you wanna be.

00:01:43.554 --> 00:01:44.847
What if it doesn't work?

00:01:45.973 --> 00:01:47.558
Well, how do you mean?

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:51.854
What if something happens
and you guys change your mind?

00:01:52.105 --> 00:01:53.606
Like what?

00:01:53.815 --> 00:01:55.733
You steal a car?
You burn down a house?

00:01:55.983 --> 00:01:58.611
You beat up the captain
of the water polo team?

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.738
Those ships have sailed, my friend.

00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:05.326
You have to promise us you'll stay out
of trouble. From now on, no more fights.

00:02:05.493 --> 00:02:11.124
You're still on probation, and Child
Services will be up our ass all the time.

00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:15.378
No more trouble. I promise.

00:02:18.256 --> 00:02:19.507
Well...

00:02:23.261 --> 00:02:26.889
- Welcome to the family.
- Thanks, guys.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.897
Okay, Seth. You can come out now.

00:02:39.902 --> 00:02:41.904
You knew about this
and didn't say anything.

00:02:42.155 --> 00:02:43.406
I didn't wanna jinx it.

00:02:44.031 --> 00:02:46.242
Dude, you're a Cohen now.

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:49.662
Welcome to a life of insecurity
and paralyzing self-doubt.

00:02:49.912 --> 00:02:54.167
Yeah. Now all I have to do
is stay out of trouble.

00:02:55.626 --> 00:02:57.295
Yeah, that could be...

00:02:57.545 --> 00:02:58.921
...difficult.

00:03:36.042 --> 00:03:39.796
You're gonna need
bedding and towels.

00:03:41.047 --> 00:03:43.716
How's the bed, Ryan?
Is it comfortable?

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:45.718
Yeah, it's...

00:03:49.222 --> 00:03:51.224
It's fine. It's great.

00:03:52.308 --> 00:03:55.728
We want you to have your privacy,
but it's a pool house. It needs warmth.

00:03:55.978 --> 00:03:58.856
You'll need chairs and a desk,
a bookshelf...

00:03:59.107 --> 00:04:01.943
Plasma flat screen,
a couple of turntables, minibar.

00:04:02.193 --> 00:04:06.114
And we should clean all this out so that
you have room for some of your...

00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:10.952
Right, you don't have stuff, so we have
to buy clothes, shoes and underpants.

00:04:11.119 --> 00:04:13.204
Mom, don't say "underpants."

00:04:14.247 --> 00:04:15.998
I've got everything I need. Really.

00:04:16.249 --> 00:04:19.460
I bet you don't have a tux.
Because you're gonna need one.

00:04:20.128 --> 00:04:21.879
- For what?
- For cotillion.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:25.383
It's the annual debutante ball.
It's Newport's biggest event.

00:04:25.633 --> 00:04:26.884
Until whatever's next week.

00:04:27.135 --> 00:04:29.887
It's the day when Newport's
most accomplished young women...

00:04:30.138 --> 00:04:31.639
...make their debut into society.

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:34.517
Or another excuse for them
to get wasted and throw up.

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:38.646
I was a deb. I made my debut at this
very country club not so many years ago.

00:04:38.855 --> 00:04:41.649
- The year was...
- Hey, watch it.

00:04:44.652 --> 00:04:46.154
You know what?

00:04:47.739 --> 00:04:50.241
- Maybe I should skip it.
- You have to go.

00:04:50.408 --> 00:04:52.994
It's a family tradition.
And you're part of the family.

00:04:53.161 --> 00:04:55.413
- Hello, dear.
- Hi, Peggy.

00:04:55.621 --> 00:04:57.415
- How are you?
- I'm good.

00:04:57.623 --> 00:05:00.126
- How's it going?
- It will be fine.

00:05:00.293 --> 00:05:03.796
- The fitting area's back there.
- Thank you.

00:05:04.047 --> 00:05:06.132
Come on, boys. It'll be fun.

00:05:19.187 --> 00:05:20.646
Sandy.

00:05:20.813 --> 00:05:22.315
Hey, Jimmy.

00:05:23.524 --> 00:05:25.318
Got some surfing in, huh?

00:05:25.526 --> 00:05:28.404
Late court date. Gotta take advantage.

00:05:28.571 --> 00:05:30.656
I used to have hobbies.

00:05:30.823 --> 00:05:33.826
Look, I know you're not thrilled
with me.

00:05:34.077 --> 00:05:38.289
When I borrowed the money from
Kirsten, I should have asked you.

00:05:38.456 --> 00:05:41.834
- I wasn't going behind your back.
- Look, it's done. Let's move on.

00:05:42.043 --> 00:05:44.462
I was afraid of what you'd think of me.

00:05:45.963 --> 00:05:47.590
Losing as much money as I have...

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:51.594
...is not an impressive accomplishment.

00:05:53.221 --> 00:05:55.098
- How much money did you lose?
- Look...

00:05:55.431 --> 00:05:56.557
It's not important.

00:05:58.851 --> 00:06:00.978
- How'd you lose it?
- The important thing is...

00:06:01.187 --> 00:06:05.983
...I don't know what Julie and I would
do without friends like you and Kirsten.

00:06:08.194 --> 00:06:09.362
So everything's okay?

00:06:09.612 --> 00:06:12.198
Oh, yeah. Yeah. Thank you.

00:06:12.365 --> 00:06:14.575
- I'll see you around.
- See you.

00:06:18.871 --> 00:06:23.710
Okay, pick whatever you want.
We have Gucci, Armani. Versace's there.

00:06:30.091 --> 00:06:32.844
Hi, I'm picking up for Marissa Cooper.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:35.513
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:06:36.389 --> 00:06:37.974
What are you doing here?

00:06:38.141 --> 00:06:39.642
I...

00:06:39.892 --> 00:06:42.019
...had an appointment
with my personal shopper.

00:06:43.521 --> 00:06:46.274
But I thought you said
you were leaving with your mom.

00:06:47.024 --> 00:06:51.279
It didn't really work out,
so I'm kind of living with the Cohens.

00:06:52.238 --> 00:06:54.615
- For good?
- Is that...

00:06:54.782 --> 00:06:57.160
...gonna be a problem?
- No, no. It's great.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:59.495
I mean, I guess now
we can be friends, right?

00:07:01.664 --> 00:07:02.915
Hey, Coop.

00:07:03.166 --> 00:07:06.169
These gloves are giving me
serious sausage arms.

00:07:06.419 --> 00:07:09.547
What are you still doing here?
I thought you were going back to Chino.

00:07:09.797 --> 00:07:12.300
- I had a change of plans.
- Ryan's living here now.

00:07:13.384 --> 00:07:15.678
- He's what?
- Look, I'm not here to cause problems.

00:07:15.928 --> 00:07:17.305
Is everything all right?

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:21.392
- I'll be in the truck.
- Great.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:25.563
Marissa, I was gonna call you.
Since you're lead deb...

00:07:25.813 --> 00:07:27.398
Seth?

00:07:27.565 --> 00:07:30.193
I wanted to introduce you
to a couple of white knights.

00:07:30.401 --> 00:07:32.904
In case any of your girls
needed a last-minute escort.

00:07:33.071 --> 00:07:35.573
- Okay.
- Every girl needs a white knight.

00:07:36.949 --> 00:07:39.285
Seth Cohen, white knight.

00:07:41.037 --> 00:07:43.706
So you'll be at the rehearsal?

00:07:43.956 --> 00:07:45.708
Yes, absolutely.

00:07:46.793 --> 00:07:48.461
See you then.

00:07:49.545 --> 00:07:50.963
Bye.

00:07:51.172 --> 00:07:53.299
Cotillion rocks.

00:07:53.966 --> 00:07:58.054
You want me to fix you up with Ryan?
I thought you said he was a "psycho."

00:07:58.221 --> 00:08:01.224
- That was before I got to know him.
- When did you get to know him?

00:08:01.432 --> 00:08:02.600
Just now.

00:08:02.809 --> 00:08:04.977
Plus there's that
whole brooding bad-boy thing.

00:08:05.186 --> 00:08:07.313
He's wounded. I can save him.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:10.858
Have you ever really talked to him?
He's not really a bad boy.

00:08:11.067 --> 00:08:13.611
Well, he will be by the time
I get through with him.

00:08:17.365 --> 00:08:21.119
What? You're not, like,
into him, are you?

00:08:21.327 --> 00:08:23.746
- I mean, you're with Luke, right?
- Right.

00:08:23.955 --> 00:08:25.248
Good.

00:08:28.626 --> 00:08:30.378
Sandy Cohen?

00:08:30.586 --> 00:08:34.507
I'm with the Securities and Exchange
Commission, Enforcement Division.

00:08:35.717 --> 00:08:37.135
Okay.

00:08:37.385 --> 00:08:39.762
I was hoping you could help me out
with a case.

00:08:40.388 --> 00:08:42.640
Sure. What can I do for you?

00:08:43.015 --> 00:08:46.144
Were you aware, Mr. Cohen,
that a check your wife made out...

00:08:46.352 --> 00:08:50.648
...to a James Cooper for $100,000
was not treated as an investment...

00:08:50.857 --> 00:08:53.151
...but as a deposit
into his personal account?

00:08:53.359 --> 00:08:57.405
It wasn't an investment. It was a loan.
My wife and Jimmy are old...

00:08:58.656 --> 00:09:00.992
- What's this about?
- Did you know Mr. Cooper is...

00:09:01.159 --> 00:09:03.745
...the subject of an
SEC fraud investigation?

00:09:04.912 --> 00:09:06.414
No.

00:09:07.749 --> 00:09:09.250
No, I didn't.

00:09:11.878 --> 00:09:15.173
Hey. White gloves,
ready for a comeback.

00:09:15.381 --> 00:09:17.633
Hey. What are you doing home?

00:09:19.677 --> 00:09:21.679
Fellas, do you mind?

00:09:23.014 --> 00:09:25.808
- Lf this is about the vase...
- Which vase?

00:09:26.559 --> 00:09:30.313
Nothing. Let's go, Ryan.
Come on, buddy.

00:09:36.694 --> 00:09:37.904
What's going on?

00:09:40.198 --> 00:09:42.450
Okay. So...

00:09:42.825 --> 00:09:44.827
I think I'm not going to cotillion.

00:09:45.078 --> 00:09:46.829
Yeah, okay. Except that you are.

00:09:47.038 --> 00:09:50.166
I made a promise to your parents
that I'd stay out of trouble.

00:09:50.333 --> 00:09:52.835
It's a debutante ball.
What trouble can you get into?

00:09:53.044 --> 00:09:54.420
Why don't you ask Luke.

00:09:55.046 --> 00:09:57.215
Ryan, we're white knights, okay?

00:09:57.465 --> 00:10:00.593
That means Marissa probably
already has some sad, Ionely girl...

00:10:00.802 --> 00:10:04.097
...lined up for you to escort,
so you can't cancel at the last minute.

00:10:04.305 --> 00:10:05.973
That's a faux pas, buddy.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.604
- Would you call her?
- No.

00:10:12.855 --> 00:10:17.318
If you're gonna bail on Marissa and some
poor, pathetic, dateless girl...

00:10:17.485 --> 00:10:19.821
...you'll just have to
do that one yourself.

00:10:20.363 --> 00:10:21.864
Are you sure?

00:10:22.073 --> 00:10:25.576
These guys say Jimmy's been siphoning
money out of his clients' accounts...

00:10:25.743 --> 00:10:27.620
...to cover his own debts.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:33.251
- How could we not know this?
- Because we trusted him. Everybody did.

00:10:33.501 --> 00:10:36.963
This entire community wrote him blank
checks. You gave him 100 grand.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.381
It was just a loan.

00:10:38.631 --> 00:10:41.968
Which, according to the SEC,
makes us worth investigating too.

00:10:42.135 --> 00:10:44.137
I'm gonna be sick.

00:10:47.515 --> 00:10:49.851
I'm gonna have to call our friends
and let them know.

00:10:50.017 --> 00:10:53.396
Sandy, wait.
You're just gonna panic people.

00:10:53.604 --> 00:10:55.982
Don't do anything
until I talk to him, okay?

00:10:56.149 --> 00:10:58.901
Put your feelings for him aside.
Forget about your history.

00:10:59.152 --> 00:11:01.362
He's one of my oldest friends.

00:11:04.157 --> 00:11:06.784
If it's true, I just need
to hear it from him.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:10.538
I'm coming.

00:11:12.665 --> 00:11:15.043
Hey. You're...

00:11:15.251 --> 00:11:16.878
...at my house.
- I...

00:11:17.045 --> 00:11:19.672
Well, I wanted to talk to you
about cotillion.

00:11:19.881 --> 00:11:21.632
Oh. Okay, well...

00:11:21.799 --> 00:11:26.137
I was just trying this on,
and I can't seem to reach the...

00:11:26.304 --> 00:11:27.680
Did you want me to...?

00:11:28.806 --> 00:11:30.641
I could... Do you want me to...?

00:11:31.142 --> 00:11:34.562
Yeah. You know, actually,
if you wouldn't mind.

00:11:59.712 --> 00:12:01.297
Thanks.

00:12:02.048 --> 00:12:03.966
So, what's up with cotillion?

00:12:05.468 --> 00:12:07.678
What time did you want me there?

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.685
I'm... I'm so sorry.

00:12:14.852 --> 00:12:17.730
I never meant for you
to be dragged in like this.

00:12:17.939 --> 00:12:22.819
How did this happen? I understand
a couple of bad investments, but theft?

00:12:22.985 --> 00:12:25.571
- Theft? No, no.
- Okay, honey, so we're gonna...

00:12:25.738 --> 00:12:27.490
- Oh, Kirsten.
- Julie.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:32.453
- Jimmy didn't say you were coming by.
- She just had a quick business question.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.997
- A quickie, huh?
- Julie.

00:12:35.206 --> 00:12:38.626
I'm kidding. So we're off.
Kaitlin needs new shoes for cotillion.

00:12:38.835 --> 00:12:42.463
Then we're test-driving the CLK, then I
have to re-up Marissa's tennis lessons.

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:45.091
- So which credit card should I use?
- The MasterCard.

00:12:45.258 --> 00:12:48.761
- What about the Amex?
- No, don't use the Amex. The...

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:50.346
Get the miles.

00:12:51.723 --> 00:12:53.141
Okay.

00:12:53.641 --> 00:12:55.226
You two have fun.

00:12:57.478 --> 00:13:01.649
Well, now that the how and why
have been accounted for...

00:13:01.858 --> 00:13:07.029
Look, I was not stealing.
I was borrowing to pay back my debts.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:09.657
And then the market took a turn,
and there we are.

00:13:09.866 --> 00:13:11.284
You were stealing.

00:13:11.534 --> 00:13:17.040
I... I can't say no to my family.
I'll pay everything back.

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:20.668
- I just need that one stock. That one.
- Jimmy, you need help.

00:13:26.382 --> 00:13:28.634
Yeah, well, who's gonna help me?

00:13:33.681 --> 00:13:36.684
So, what exactly happens
at this rehearsal?

00:13:36.893 --> 00:13:39.062
Just stupid cotillion stuff.

00:13:39.312 --> 00:13:41.898
Bowing and curtsying.

00:13:42.065 --> 00:13:45.568
One, two, three. One, two, three.

00:13:45.818 --> 00:13:49.072
Try to enjoy this, please.

00:13:49.322 --> 00:13:51.699
Dancing? You didn't tell me
there was dancing.

00:13:51.949 --> 00:13:54.911
Well, if I'd told you there was dancing,
I'd be here by myself.

00:13:55.078 --> 00:13:56.579
Because I really...

00:13:56.829 --> 00:13:58.206
...don't dance.

00:13:58.456 --> 00:14:00.458
Neither do I. I just move well.

00:14:03.461 --> 00:14:05.588
Want me to teach you that one?

00:14:06.714 --> 00:14:09.717
- Maybe later. You ready?
- Take your places.

00:14:11.177 --> 00:14:14.305
Hey, guys.
So can I introduce you to your debs?

00:14:14.472 --> 00:14:16.182
We've already met.

00:14:16.557 --> 00:14:20.103
Oh, well, actually, Summer, Ryan's
already been promised to someone else.

00:14:20.353 --> 00:14:22.230
You gave him to someone else?

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:26.442
Who? Who's pathetic enough not
to have a date the day before cotillion?

00:14:26.609 --> 00:14:29.695
Actually, at this point,
that would be you.

00:14:29.862 --> 00:14:33.991
So, Anna Stern, this is Ryan Atwood.
Anna just moved here from Pittsburgh.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:35.743
Pittsburgh?

00:14:36.869 --> 00:14:39.247
Can we just get this over with?

00:14:41.999 --> 00:14:43.751
Caliente.

00:14:45.878 --> 00:14:49.090
- Hey, it's not that bad.
- You haven't seen me dance.

00:14:49.257 --> 00:14:51.092
Well, I can help you.

00:14:51.259 --> 00:14:53.970
So, like, what am I supposed to do?

00:14:54.137 --> 00:14:55.888
Over here.

00:14:57.849 --> 00:14:59.350
Fine. Let's go.

00:14:59.517 --> 00:15:01.644
Are you sure? Because if you're not...

00:15:01.894 --> 00:15:04.480
Just don't talk to me.

00:15:04.647 --> 00:15:08.151
All right, I get it. Our...
Our connection's deeper than words.

00:15:10.987 --> 00:15:14.240
That's it. I'm done. I'm sorry.
Chock-full of quiet now.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:19.996
Okay. So you guys will be over here.

00:15:20.163 --> 00:15:22.749
If you want to,
go ahead and get into waltz position.

00:15:24.917 --> 00:15:28.421
Which means, Anna, you put
your left hand on Ryan's shoulder.

00:15:30.631 --> 00:15:33.051
No, not like that. Here, watch.

00:15:35.303 --> 00:15:38.931
Okay? Now, Ryan, you put
your right hand on my back.

00:15:39.557 --> 00:15:41.309
Lower.

00:16:01.454 --> 00:16:03.456
Okay. Good.

00:16:03.956 --> 00:16:05.208
Good.

00:16:05.416 --> 00:16:07.085
I'd be pretty jealous right now...

00:16:08.461 --> 00:16:09.962
...if Chino wasn't gay.

00:16:10.838 --> 00:16:12.673
- Luke.
- What? No, it doesn't bother me.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.175
He was born that way, right?

00:16:14.342 --> 00:16:16.469
Thanks. I think
we can take it from here.

00:16:16.677 --> 00:16:18.346
Okay.

00:16:22.725 --> 00:16:23.851
You're into her, huh?

00:16:25.478 --> 00:16:27.313
Man, are you in trouble.

00:16:28.106 --> 00:16:29.690
- I know.
- Yeah.

00:16:29.857 --> 00:16:31.317
- Yeah.
- Come on.

00:16:36.114 --> 00:16:38.074
All right, darlings, listen up.

00:16:38.241 --> 00:16:41.744
Let's review the classic waltz step.
Phillip?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.122
And...

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.707
One, two, three.

00:16:45.873 --> 00:16:47.250
One, two, three.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:49.085
One, two, three.

00:16:49.252 --> 00:16:51.379
One, two, three. Smile, please.

00:16:51.629 --> 00:16:55.633
- That kid is stalking you.
- He is not. He's my neighbor.

00:16:55.842 --> 00:16:58.094
And he's not going anywhere,
so get used to him.

00:16:58.261 --> 00:17:02.974
What I'll never get used to is that kid
macking on you when I turn my back.

00:17:03.141 --> 00:17:05.393
So you don't trust me?

00:17:06.352 --> 00:17:07.895
No, I...

00:17:09.272 --> 00:17:13.401
I don't trust anybody else.
Not around you.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.867
- Wait.
- Slow down.

00:17:21.117 --> 00:17:23.619
Are you the kid from Chino
who steals cars...

00:17:23.786 --> 00:17:26.164
...and sets people's houses on fire?

00:17:28.291 --> 00:17:32.420
You're saying I'm making my debut into
society with Newport's most wanted?

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:35.048
- Is that gonna be a problem?
- I can't wait.

00:17:39.052 --> 00:17:40.928
Absolutely not.

00:17:41.179 --> 00:17:45.558
As happy as I am that you came all
the way out to my office to visit me...

00:17:46.768 --> 00:17:47.810
...the answer is no.

00:17:48.019 --> 00:17:51.939
Corey! I need that file
on Nerodner v. Caplin.

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:54.817
- And I need the INS report on my 4:30.
- Yes, sir.

00:17:55.068 --> 00:17:57.904
I got a two-time drug offender
they want to deport. 15 years old.

00:17:58.071 --> 00:17:59.697
Sandy, he needs help.

00:17:59.947 --> 00:18:03.201
Jimmy Cooper? He stole from his clients,
he stole from his friends...

00:18:03.409 --> 00:18:07.580
...and then he had the nerve to borrow
$100,000 from us to cover it up.

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:10.208
He was trying to provide for his family.

00:18:10.416 --> 00:18:11.834
Yeah. Boats, ponies...

00:18:12.043 --> 00:18:14.587
- You'll defend a drug offender, but...?
- Yes.

00:18:14.962 --> 00:18:19.467
My clients are kids who have
no hope, no guidance, nothing.

00:18:19.675 --> 00:18:23.221
Jimmy Cooper is just another
spoiled Newport brat...

00:18:23.429 --> 00:18:25.098
...who had everything handed to him.

00:18:25.306 --> 00:18:27.600
- Like me.
- No. Not like you.

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:30.937
You would never lie.
You would never steal.

00:18:31.104 --> 00:18:33.231
I'd like to think that, but the truth is...

00:18:33.481 --> 00:18:36.442
...there isn't anything
that I wouldn't do for my family.

00:18:36.984 --> 00:18:38.611
See you at home.

00:18:43.866 --> 00:18:47.203
- Three hours of dancing.
- I feel like I could go for three more.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.330
Ryan. So Anna seemed nice.

00:18:49.497 --> 00:18:52.125
I mean, I just figured she's new
and you're new, so...

00:18:52.333 --> 00:18:56.212
- Yeah.
- Great. Good.

00:18:57.004 --> 00:18:59.716
Holl, I was about to tell them
about the cookout tonight.

00:18:59.882 --> 00:19:02.343
It's at my house.
I do it every year for cotillion.

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:05.221
- You didn't do it last year.
- Yeah, we did.

00:19:07.348 --> 00:19:08.349
Ouch.

00:19:08.516 --> 00:19:09.767
- See you tonight.
- Bye.

00:19:10.017 --> 00:19:11.352
See you there.

00:19:11.519 --> 00:19:13.771
You really think
that's such a great idea?

00:19:15.273 --> 00:19:16.649
Yeah, I do.

00:19:16.858 --> 00:19:21.028
You're living here now, and there's no
reason why we all can't hang out, right?

00:19:23.656 --> 00:19:26.409
- I can think of a reason.
- Yeah. I'm not going.

00:19:26.617 --> 00:19:28.911
- I don't want to go alone.
- Summer will be there.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:32.623
Yeah, I'm still going. I would just prefer
not to go alone. Listen to me.

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:36.794
We're like brothers now, okay?
That means we do stuff for each other.

00:19:37.003 --> 00:19:40.673
If you do this for me, later on
I'll be able to do something for you.

00:19:40.882 --> 00:19:44.302
I don't know what it's going to be yet,
but it's gonna be awesome.

00:19:44.761 --> 00:19:45.762
Please?

00:19:45.928 --> 00:19:49.015
Okay, here we are.
Thank you very much. Okay.

00:19:49.182 --> 00:19:52.685
Here we go, sweetheart.
Make sure we got everything.

00:19:52.894 --> 00:19:56.314
Hey, Jimmy Cooper.
Just the man I wanted to see.

00:19:56.522 --> 00:19:58.816
- Hey, Greg. Hey, Holly.
- Hey, Mr. Cooper.

00:19:59.025 --> 00:20:00.193
Somebody's having a party.

00:20:00.443 --> 00:20:03.154
Holly's hosting this thing for the debs
out at the beach house.

00:20:03.321 --> 00:20:06.199
That's right. Marissa's going.
Have a good time.

00:20:06.449 --> 00:20:09.285
Honey, take these down to the car.
I'll be right there. Okay?

00:20:09.452 --> 00:20:12.163
Hi, I'm picking up for Cooper.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:15.666
Listen, Jimmy. I haven't heard back
from you. Did you get my messages?

00:20:15.833 --> 00:20:16.959
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:20:17.168 --> 00:20:20.463
You know, work has been so crazy.
But what's going on?

00:20:20.713 --> 00:20:23.674
I've been asked to invest
in a commercial real-estate property.

00:20:23.841 --> 00:20:25.802
It could be a nice second income for us.

00:20:25.968 --> 00:20:29.472
It might be our only income, the way
the pharmaceutical industry's going.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:32.100
- That sounds promising.
- Yeah.

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:36.562
So we're gonna have to pull $250,000
out of the investment account.

00:20:38.981 --> 00:20:42.610
Are you sure you wanna do that,
with the market about to turn around?

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:47.240
Sir? I'm sorry,
but your credit card's been declined.

00:20:50.493 --> 00:20:54.330
Oh, it's a new card,
and I forgot to activate it.

00:20:54.497 --> 00:20:56.374
Did you want to use another card?

00:20:57.375 --> 00:20:59.252
Dad, I'm gonna be late
to my own party.

00:20:59.502 --> 00:21:00.712
Okay, honey.

00:21:00.878 --> 00:21:04.882
I'll call you tomorrow about the details.
Just bring the check to the cotillion.

00:21:05.133 --> 00:21:06.634
Enjoy your meal.

00:21:11.013 --> 00:21:13.474
I'll just pay with cash.

00:21:18.646 --> 00:21:20.982
Give me 10 minutes to find Summer,
lock it down for tomorrow.

00:21:21.149 --> 00:21:22.275
See where the night takes me.

00:21:22.525 --> 00:21:25.153
- Better take you back here in 10 minutes.
- Don't wait up.

00:21:25.403 --> 00:21:28.656
Come on. Two Jack Johnson tickets,
a massage at Burke Williams...

00:21:28.906 --> 00:21:33.244
...and all the money I have on me,
which is $11.

00:21:33.411 --> 00:21:35.872
Sorry, Summer,
I don't want to trade escorts.

00:21:36.998 --> 00:21:40.168
- Hey, Summer.
- What did I say about talking to me?

00:21:40.376 --> 00:21:45.423
Okay. I just wanted to make sure
we're still on for tomorrow night.

00:21:45.673 --> 00:21:47.175
I guess.

00:21:47.383 --> 00:21:50.803
Could you even pretend
to be a little bit stoked?

00:21:51.679 --> 00:21:53.306
Fair enough.

00:21:53.556 --> 00:21:56.934
You're a really good barbecue-tionist.

00:22:02.774 --> 00:22:04.275
There it is.

00:22:05.777 --> 00:22:07.445
Oh, jeez!

00:22:11.324 --> 00:22:14.077
You lost a bet. You lost a bet.
You've got to pay up.

00:22:26.339 --> 00:22:28.091
You sure you want to be seen with me?

00:22:28.341 --> 00:22:32.970
Hey, I'm glad you came. I mean,
how could you possibly miss all this?

00:22:36.849 --> 00:22:40.103
- I'm gonna go.
- Hey, we're not doing anything wrong.

00:22:40.353 --> 00:22:44.190
Well, now that you've moved in, I see
you're making yourself right at home.

00:22:44.357 --> 00:22:46.484
Luke, come on.
You said you were gonna try.

00:22:46.692 --> 00:22:50.988
I'm trying. I'm trying to understand
why there's all these people here...

00:22:51.197 --> 00:22:54.742
...and you only want to talk to her.
- Hey, I wanted to talk to him.

00:22:54.992 --> 00:22:58.496
Look, babe, why don't you go talk
to Summer, all right? She looks Ionely.

00:22:58.746 --> 00:23:01.249
Or you can,
and I'll finish talking to Ryan.

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.253
No, it's okay. I'm just gonna go.

00:23:05.461 --> 00:23:08.005
- No. Stay.
- What are you doing? Don't tell him that.

00:23:08.214 --> 00:23:11.634
- Don't tell her what to do.
- I thought you were leaving.

00:23:11.843 --> 00:23:13.761
Why don't I just help you out.

00:23:17.515 --> 00:23:18.891
I'm not gonna fight.

00:23:21.728 --> 00:23:24.021
- Even if I do this?
- Luke!

00:23:25.148 --> 00:23:27.024
Oh, God. Are you okay?

00:23:28.651 --> 00:23:30.987
God, Luke, you're such an idiot.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:36.909
You just got your butt kicked and didn't
fight back. Dude, you really are a Cohen.

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:38.786
Yeah. Let's get you home.

00:23:51.549 --> 00:23:53.885
What are you doing?
Why aren't you dressed yet?

00:23:54.052 --> 00:23:57.430
I'm not going. Would you let Anna know?
She'll probably be relieved.

00:23:57.638 --> 00:23:59.891
Are you not going
because you're afraid of Luke?

00:24:00.058 --> 00:24:02.310
That's not what I'm afraid of.

00:24:04.062 --> 00:24:08.524
Look, your parents taking me in is the
greatest thing that's happened to me.

00:24:08.691 --> 00:24:11.569
I'm not gonna lose it
just to kick some guy's ass.

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:15.406
- You could totally kick his ass, right?
- Oh, yeah.

00:24:15.573 --> 00:24:17.033
Cool.

00:24:18.701 --> 00:24:21.037
All right. Well...

00:24:22.455 --> 00:24:23.956
...have fun.

00:24:28.086 --> 00:24:30.963
Sweetie, I need to borrow
your lip gloss.

00:24:31.172 --> 00:24:33.841
Oh, I love this dress.

00:24:34.092 --> 00:24:36.552
Really? Maybe you should wear it.

00:24:36.719 --> 00:24:41.224
You're sweet, but I think we both know
I'm no longer a size 0.

00:24:41.474 --> 00:24:43.851
Give me a few more months
on the Zone.

00:24:44.060 --> 00:24:46.229
I don't think I want to go.

00:24:46.437 --> 00:24:50.108
I'm sorry, I thought I heard you say you
don't want to go to your own cotillion.

00:24:50.316 --> 00:24:52.860
Look, Luke and I
got in a fight last night, okay?

00:24:53.069 --> 00:24:55.446
So you got into a fight.
You've had fights before.

00:24:55.613 --> 00:24:57.365
You guys have been together forever.

00:24:57.615 --> 00:24:59.992
Maybe that's the problem.

00:25:01.369 --> 00:25:04.622
I mean, what if
there's someone else out there?

00:25:04.831 --> 00:25:06.999
Like who? That boy from Chino?

00:25:10.628 --> 00:25:14.632
Do you want to end up like Aunt Cindy,
with four kids in a trailer park?

00:25:14.841 --> 00:25:16.634
She broke my mom's heart.
You won't break mine.

00:25:16.884 --> 00:25:20.096
- So now this is about you?
- No, sweetie, it's about you.

00:25:20.263 --> 00:25:23.391
- What future is there with that boy?
- Mom, I'm 16.

00:25:23.641 --> 00:25:27.270
The choices you make when you're 16
can affect your entire future.

00:25:27.478 --> 00:25:31.983
Luke is from a good family. If you stay
with him, you'll always be comfortable.

00:25:32.150 --> 00:25:35.903
- I'm comfortable now.
- Nothing in life is certain.

00:25:37.405 --> 00:25:40.241
- What does that mean?
- It means you'll put on this dress...

00:25:40.408 --> 00:25:44.662
...do your hair like I showed you and
make your debut into society with Luke.

00:25:44.871 --> 00:25:46.164
I can't.

00:25:48.916 --> 00:25:50.293
I'm sorry.

00:25:51.502 --> 00:25:52.545
No, you're not.

00:25:54.047 --> 00:25:56.257
But you will be.

00:26:03.389 --> 00:26:05.683
What are you doing?
Why aren't you dressed?

00:26:05.892 --> 00:26:08.311
- I'm not going.
- What do you mean, you're not going?

00:26:08.561 --> 00:26:10.438
I don't feel like getting dressed up...

00:26:10.646 --> 00:26:13.191
...and pretending Jimmy Cooper
is the O.C. Golden boy.

00:26:14.067 --> 00:26:18.029
And any community that makes that guy
a hero is not one I feel like being part of.

00:26:18.946 --> 00:26:20.073
You're not going either?

00:26:20.323 --> 00:26:23.076
- I wanted to leave 20 minutes ago.
- Let's go.

00:26:23.284 --> 00:26:26.162
- Dad, why aren't you...?
- Seth. Now.

00:26:28.915 --> 00:26:31.667
I don't know.
Maybe I shouldn't go either.

00:26:31.834 --> 00:26:35.171
What? What is wrong with this family?

00:26:35.338 --> 00:26:38.674
This is cotillion, the most
important event of the year.

00:26:38.841 --> 00:26:40.676
Am I the only one who gets it?

00:26:40.843 --> 00:26:42.678
I get it, Mommy.

00:26:42.845 --> 00:26:45.807
Daddy, it's Mr. Fisher again.
He's called, like, three times.

00:26:45.973 --> 00:26:49.227
No. We do not have time
for you two to talk business.

00:26:49.435 --> 00:26:53.314
Tell Greg Daddy will see him
at the cotillion. Right, Jimmy?

00:26:55.233 --> 00:26:57.360
All right.

00:26:57.610 --> 00:27:00.071
Come on. We don't wanna be late.

00:27:05.493 --> 00:27:07.495
You guys know Anna Stern?

00:27:07.704 --> 00:27:09.122
Seth.

00:27:11.082 --> 00:27:12.208
Wow.

00:27:13.751 --> 00:27:16.713
- You think?
- Yes...

00:27:16.879 --> 00:27:21.008
...I do. Which makes this
even harder to say.

00:27:21.217 --> 00:27:25.888
Anna, just know that, in life,
there are peaks and...

00:27:26.097 --> 00:27:27.640
Ryan's not coming, is he?

00:27:27.849 --> 00:27:30.727
Kind of took the wind
out of my sails there, but yes.

00:27:32.478 --> 00:27:35.148
- Are you okay?
- I'll survive.

00:27:44.615 --> 00:27:47.243
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:27:47.910 --> 00:27:50.163
- Thought you were going to cotillion.
- I thought you were.

00:27:50.413 --> 00:27:53.249
Yeah. No.

00:27:54.542 --> 00:27:56.544
Yeah, me neither.

00:27:57.420 --> 00:28:00.298
- Which one's sword?
- Not the one you're hitting.

00:28:00.548 --> 00:28:03.301
- Got it.
- Okay, now you're stabbing me.

00:28:03.551 --> 00:28:06.929
Just don't touch any of the buttons.
Follow me through the forest...

00:28:07.180 --> 00:28:10.016
...and maybe we'll both make it
out of here alive.

00:28:11.768 --> 00:28:14.187
So you didn't feel like going, huh?

00:28:14.395 --> 00:28:17.273
Yeah. No, not really for me.

00:28:17.440 --> 00:28:20.818
What? Waltzing and orchids?
What could be more you?

00:28:21.069 --> 00:28:23.029
Guess I don't really fit in, huh?

00:28:23.196 --> 00:28:25.531
Oh, I got news for you. Nobody does.

00:28:26.699 --> 00:28:30.578
I guarantee you every single person
at that cotillion feels like a fraud.

00:28:30.828 --> 00:28:34.665
They've all got secrets, and they're all
terrified the neighbors will find out.

00:28:35.583 --> 00:28:37.335
What's your secret?

00:28:38.461 --> 00:28:43.841
Sometimes, when the sun's
coming up and the surf is good...

00:28:44.092 --> 00:28:48.221
...and I haven't pissed my wife off
quite as much as I have today...

00:28:49.347 --> 00:28:51.182
...I kind of like this place.

00:28:52.975 --> 00:28:54.685
You just stabbed me again.

00:28:55.728 --> 00:28:56.979
Sorry.

00:28:57.188 --> 00:28:58.731
I can't believe you're not coming.

00:28:58.940 --> 00:29:03.694
It's just after the whole Luke and Ryan
thing last night, I don't feel...

00:29:03.861 --> 00:29:05.238
Coop...

00:29:05.488 --> 00:29:06.739
...Ryan isn't even here.

00:29:07.115 --> 00:29:08.491
He's not?

00:29:09.492 --> 00:29:11.828
Yeah, well, even so.

00:29:12.495 --> 00:29:13.871
I'm just not up for it.

00:29:16.874 --> 00:29:18.584
She's not coming.

00:29:20.002 --> 00:29:22.130
So, what did I get all dressed up for?

00:29:34.642 --> 00:29:37.895
I mean, whatever you think about
the whole superhero movie genre...

00:29:38.146 --> 00:29:40.732
...at least people are now reading
the source material.

00:29:40.898 --> 00:29:45.611
I cannot believe that you read
comic books. I mean, you're a girl.

00:29:45.778 --> 00:29:48.781
What's that supposed to mean?
And I call them "graphic novels."

00:29:48.990 --> 00:29:52.493
In fact, if more people did, maybe
the form wouldn't be so marginalized.

00:29:52.660 --> 00:29:54.662
I couldn't agree more.

00:29:56.247 --> 00:29:59.292
Summer, are you ready?
You look just great.

00:29:59.542 --> 00:30:01.044
So listen...

00:30:06.799 --> 00:30:08.426
You...

00:30:09.177 --> 00:30:10.928
...found another date.
- Yeah.

00:30:11.179 --> 00:30:14.182
It's kind of an emergency,
but you're off the hook.

00:30:15.433 --> 00:30:18.144
- Sorry.
- No, that's...

00:30:22.315 --> 00:30:24.025
That's fine.

00:30:38.956 --> 00:30:41.334
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:30:43.419 --> 00:30:44.670
You're not at cotillion.

00:30:45.463 --> 00:30:46.714
Neither are you.

00:30:50.218 --> 00:30:53.846
Look, I hope you didn't not go
because of last night or...

00:30:54.305 --> 00:30:55.848
...because of me.

00:30:58.351 --> 00:30:59.727
How come you're not going?

00:31:03.564 --> 00:31:06.859
So you think hiding out, staying home
is gonna make everything better?

00:31:07.610 --> 00:31:09.946
Seems to be working for you.

00:31:13.116 --> 00:31:15.368
I'll go if you go.

00:31:17.203 --> 00:31:21.124
Ryan, come on. Check this out. I have
totally annihilated all the other ninjas.

00:31:21.374 --> 00:31:23.126
I'm already on to the...

00:31:23.710 --> 00:31:25.378
Marissa. Hello.

00:31:25.878 --> 00:31:27.380
Hey.

00:31:28.214 --> 00:31:29.882
So we're gonna go.

00:31:30.967 --> 00:31:32.135
To cotillion.

00:31:36.264 --> 00:31:37.390
I'll get the car.

00:31:42.520 --> 00:31:44.981
Hey, Jimmy, there you are.

00:31:45.148 --> 00:31:48.359
- Greg, how you doing?
- I'll be better once I get that check...

00:31:48.526 --> 00:31:51.487
...get this property deal closed,
get my wife off my back.

00:31:51.654 --> 00:31:54.907
- I don't have it.
- What do you mean? Did you forget it?

00:31:55.116 --> 00:31:59.037
This isn't the time or place. Stop by the
office tomorrow, and we'll talk about it.

00:31:59.245 --> 00:32:01.372
Talk about it? Talk about what?

00:32:08.254 --> 00:32:11.049
- Excuse me.
- Jimmy...

00:32:13.885 --> 00:32:16.012
I don't believe it.

00:32:20.933 --> 00:32:24.270
You told Summer you weren't coming.
Now you're here with him?

00:32:24.437 --> 00:32:26.939
- Ryan and I aren't here together.
- I'm not an idiot.

00:32:27.148 --> 00:32:29.192
Then listen to her
and stop acting like one.

00:32:29.400 --> 00:32:31.027
What did you say?

00:32:31.569 --> 00:32:34.572
- Forget it.
- No, what did you say? Come on, man.

00:32:34.822 --> 00:32:36.324
Luke, stop it.

00:32:39.952 --> 00:32:42.580
I'm over this. We're done.

00:33:01.849 --> 00:33:04.727
Hey, look who decided to show up.

00:33:04.977 --> 00:33:08.439
Don't worry, your hit man already
took care of it. I didn't feel a thing.

00:33:09.065 --> 00:33:10.566
I'm here now, if you want to...

00:33:11.234 --> 00:33:13.861
No, too late. You missed your shot.

00:33:14.112 --> 00:33:17.824
I guess you'll have to go
with Princess Mononoke over there.

00:33:19.117 --> 00:33:22.829
- And what are you gonna do?
- Oh, so now you care? Go.

00:33:24.706 --> 00:33:28.334
Marissa, if you'd just stuck
to the original plan...

00:33:29.502 --> 00:33:32.255
- Sorry. Do you want Daddy to go find...?
- No, Mom.

00:33:32.505 --> 00:33:36.384
- You can't debut without an escort.
- I hear there's a white knight available.

00:33:39.095 --> 00:33:43.141
Well, that's very nice of you to offer,
but I don't think it's appropriate.

00:33:43.349 --> 00:33:44.976
I'll go get dressed.

00:33:53.484 --> 00:33:55.528
Could you be any more pathetic?

00:33:56.028 --> 00:33:58.239
A Ione figure sitting on the floor...

00:33:58.406 --> 00:34:01.409
...wondering if he'll be Ionely
for the rest of his life.

00:34:02.035 --> 00:34:04.662
Hey, your sensitivity, it's really...

00:34:04.871 --> 00:34:08.374
...nonexistent.
- You know what your problem is?

00:34:09.542 --> 00:34:11.669
You're not a man.

00:34:11.919 --> 00:34:13.880
Again, not appreciating
the brutal honesty.

00:34:14.047 --> 00:34:15.882
Do you know what girls find sexy?

00:34:16.049 --> 00:34:18.551
Nope. Wait, let me guess.

00:34:18.801 --> 00:34:23.181
- Dudes who play water polo.
- Confidence. Watch this.

00:34:24.807 --> 00:34:27.310
- Seth?
- Yes?

00:34:27.518 --> 00:34:30.063
I don't have a date to the cotillion.

00:34:30.688 --> 00:34:32.523
Would you be my escort?

00:34:34.275 --> 00:34:36.027
I mean...

00:34:36.194 --> 00:34:38.821
Confidence, Cohen.

00:34:40.782 --> 00:34:42.825
Let's do this.

00:34:43.076 --> 00:34:47.955
Hair's good, makeup's good. Very nice.
Stand up straight. Gum, please.

00:34:48.206 --> 00:34:49.207
How did this happen?

00:34:49.415 --> 00:34:52.710
How did I go from having three dates
to cotillion to having none?

00:34:52.919 --> 00:34:55.338
I'm sorry, girl. That blows.

00:34:59.050 --> 00:35:00.843
Good news. I'm available again.

00:35:01.344 --> 00:35:02.929
You are?

00:35:05.932 --> 00:35:09.102
No. No. We're gonna go this way. No.

00:35:20.571 --> 00:35:23.741
Five hundred channels and nothing on.

00:35:24.742 --> 00:35:26.994
You couldn't put on a tux?

00:35:27.245 --> 00:35:29.706
Pick your battles, honey.

00:35:30.373 --> 00:35:32.333
Good evening, everyone.

00:35:32.500 --> 00:35:38.715
And welcome to the 47th annual
Newport Beach Debutante Cotillion.

00:35:47.098 --> 00:35:48.391
Hey.

00:35:50.852 --> 00:35:52.770
Are you ready to make your debut?

00:35:58.860 --> 00:36:03.114
Holly Fisher,
daughter of Greg and Marianne Fisher.

00:36:13.166 --> 00:36:17.754
Anna Stern,
daughter of Cameron and Patricia Stern.

00:36:32.393 --> 00:36:36.814
Marissa Cooper,
daughter of James and Julie Cooper.

00:36:38.900 --> 00:36:42.070
- I love you, kiddo.
- I love you too, Daddy.

00:37:11.349 --> 00:37:12.850
And now, ladies and gentlemen...

00:37:13.059 --> 00:37:17.563
...please join me in congratulating
this year's debutantes.

00:37:58.896 --> 00:38:00.898
We never finished our conversation.

00:38:01.149 --> 00:38:03.401
I gotta tell you,
you got me a little concerned.

00:38:03.651 --> 00:38:06.904
Believe me, it's nothing
that can't wait until tomorrow.

00:38:08.156 --> 00:38:09.782
Don't the girls look beautiful?

00:38:10.491 --> 00:38:12.368
I hate dancing.

00:38:12.535 --> 00:38:13.745
Thanks.

00:38:13.911 --> 00:38:16.664
No, with you, it's...

00:38:16.914 --> 00:38:19.000
It's not horrible.

00:38:19.542 --> 00:38:21.377
You're sweet.

00:38:21.544 --> 00:38:25.173
- Are you leading?
- I'm trying.

00:38:25.423 --> 00:38:28.176
Attitude. I like that.

00:38:28.384 --> 00:38:32.055
I've put in an offer. I got a mortgage,
the kids are in private school.

00:38:32.305 --> 00:38:34.140
If there's a problem, I need to know.

00:38:34.307 --> 00:38:36.434
Now is not the time.

00:38:37.643 --> 00:38:38.811
Jimmy, where's my money?

00:38:40.021 --> 00:38:41.898
I asked you a question.
Where's my money?

00:38:42.065 --> 00:38:44.901
I didn't want you to find out
this way, but I don't have it.

00:38:45.068 --> 00:38:47.195
- What?
- I will, but I don't have it right now.

00:38:47.445 --> 00:38:50.198
- Lf you don't have my money, who does?
- Hey, look.

00:38:52.325 --> 00:38:55.828
I promise I'm working on it, all right?
There's been some bad investments.

00:38:56.079 --> 00:38:57.955
Are you telling me you lost everything?

00:38:58.414 --> 00:38:59.832
Would you just keep it down?

00:39:00.083 --> 00:39:03.711
I won't keep it down. That is my money.
My retirement, my kids' tuition!

00:39:03.920 --> 00:39:06.339
- I'm sorry.
- Son of a bitch!

00:39:07.465 --> 00:39:11.302
- Oh, my God.
- You're a thief! You took my money!

00:39:11.469 --> 00:39:12.804
Greg!

00:39:13.721 --> 00:39:16.599
I want my money back, you hear me?

00:39:16.849 --> 00:39:18.601
Get off me!

00:39:18.976 --> 00:39:20.978
You're a thief! You're a thief!

00:39:21.229 --> 00:39:22.355
- Get off me.
- Go outside.

00:39:22.605 --> 00:39:24.732
- He's a thief! You're a thief!
- Leave. Please.

00:39:24.941 --> 00:39:26.109
- Come on.
- He's a thief!

00:39:26.317 --> 00:39:27.860
Dad!

00:39:28.069 --> 00:39:29.737
Take it outside. Come on.

00:39:36.369 --> 00:39:38.204
I haven't seen you
in a fight since...

00:39:38.371 --> 00:39:40.581
...ever.
- Now you know why.

00:39:40.748 --> 00:39:43.626
What are you talking about?
He sucker-punched you.

00:39:44.627 --> 00:39:47.880
You didn't have to jump in like that,
defend Jimmy.

00:39:48.089 --> 00:39:50.383
Well, I've always had this thing
for the underdog.

00:39:51.634 --> 00:39:56.848
After I fill out the police report, maybe
we should go and see how he's doing.

00:39:58.266 --> 00:39:59.892
Hi.

00:40:02.145 --> 00:40:05.523
So, sorry. I know I promised
I wouldn't get into any fights.

00:40:05.773 --> 00:40:08.526
We can make an exception
in this case.

00:40:08.735 --> 00:40:12.530
The police, however, will have questions.
As your attorney, I advise you...

00:40:13.364 --> 00:40:15.908
...get out of here.
- Thanks.

00:40:19.287 --> 00:40:20.663
Hey.

00:40:22.790 --> 00:40:25.877
You don't mind if I walk
your date home, do you?

00:40:28.171 --> 00:40:29.797
- No.
- Cool.

00:40:30.048 --> 00:40:34.052
That's quite a debut you had tonight.
You know how to present yourself.

00:40:34.260 --> 00:40:37.055
Finally, a Cohen who can throw down.

00:40:37.305 --> 00:40:38.890
You wanna come with us?

00:40:39.932 --> 00:40:42.935
- I'll just see you at home.
- See you at home.

00:40:48.316 --> 00:40:51.694
So do you think
that I'll get to see you again?

00:40:52.695 --> 00:40:54.822
- No.
- Okay.

00:40:55.031 --> 00:40:56.324
No, it's just...

00:40:56.574 --> 00:40:58.576
I know this might sound kind of...

00:40:58.826 --> 00:41:00.578
...whatever...

00:41:00.787 --> 00:41:03.664
...but I'm spending the rest
of the summer on a sailing trip.

00:41:03.831 --> 00:41:06.042
To Tahiti.

00:41:06.209 --> 00:41:09.545
- You like sailing?
- Yeah.

00:41:49.961 --> 00:41:51.629
You okay?

00:41:54.757 --> 00:41:56.718
What happened in there?

00:41:59.095 --> 00:42:00.888
I don't know.

00:42:02.640 --> 00:42:04.851
What's gonna happen now?

00:42:09.772 --> 00:42:11.274
I don't know.

00:42:17.739 --> 00:42:19.615
Come on, let's go.

00:42:21.242 --> 00:42:22.535
Come on.

00:42:30.293 --> 00:42:31.669
Came as soon as I heard.

00:42:36.424 --> 00:42:38.134
Are you...?

00:42:42.055 --> 00:42:43.556
I'm sorry.

00:42:45.641 --> 00:42:47.935
Can I take you home?

00:42:49.771 --> 00:42:52.315
- We could talk, maybe.
- I...

00:42:53.066 --> 00:42:55.026
I just need to be alone right now.

00:42:58.780 --> 00:43:00.198
Thanks.
